    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d939">

                <pb facs="0750" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/8155</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Collector Cobb to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-14T11:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1916, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My August 25, 5 p.m. Agent here has letter from employee at Parral dated October
                    4.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>They are still working the Jesus Maria. They have 18 sets of drillers and
                        about 35 other men at work making in all about 72 men. They have about two
                        cars of ore out which they are going to ship to Monterey.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
